DTSTART:20251011T021500Z
DTEND:20251011T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20251011T021500Z
UID:t7UDxB2ROo
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nOscar® nominee and onetime Washi
 ngton resident Lily Gladstone (Killers of the Flower Moon) narrates this s
 oul-stirring and tradition-oriented documentary about Montana’s Blackfoo
 t tribe as they seek to reinstate a wild buffalo herd back to their ancest
 ral land.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/bring-them-home
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinema Dissection: Cinephile's Spooky Choice
DTSTART:20251011T170000Z
DTEND:20251011T232000Z
DTSTAMP:20251011T170000Z
UID:GQ7JSWwp2L
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 360 mins (6h00m)\n\nFilm Talks You're the programmer
 ! Help choose the film for our spooky Cinema Dissection. Vote by September
  15\, and the winning selection will be announced on October 1. This year 
 SIFF celebrates the Halloween spooky season by allowing our audience membe
 rs to determine which horror genre classic will be the subject for our Oct
 ober cinema dissection. Will it be Robert Eggers’s American Gothic debut
  feature film\, The Witch? Perhaps you prefer David Robert Mitchell’s pa
 ranoid supernatural chiller\, It Follows? Maybe John Landis’s consummate
  blend of terror\, gore\, and comedy\, An American Werewolf in London? Or 
 The Hunger\, Tony Scott’s erotic revisionist vampire thriller? Whichever
  film wins the vote\, join facilitator and SIFF Programmer Dan Doody for a
  scene-by-scene deconstruction of a terrifying classic film guaranteed to 
 haunt your nightmares. Vote\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/ed
 ucation/adult-film-education/film-talks/cinema-dissection-cinephiles-choic
 e-spooky
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
